# Allowlist approach: ignore everything by default, then explicitly
# un-ignore exactly what docker/Dockerfile's COPY instructions need
# (Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/, migrations/). This is deliberately
# self-maintaining — new top-level dirs (web/, mobile/, docs, etc.) never
# leak into the build context by accident; nothing needs updating here
# unless the Dockerfile itself starts COPYing something new.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock

!crates
!crates/**

!migrations
!migrations/**

# Still exclude build output / caches even inside the allowlisted paths
target/
**/target/
